(If you’d prefer not to be notified about score changes in the future, type
NOTIFY OFF.)

>n
At the Workbench
This workbench, in the northwest part of the studio, was where you would create
works of art.  Now you just come here to contemplate your creation’s beauty,
dress her up, ply her with gifts, and lament your hopeless situation.

The statue stands on a plinth beside the workbench.

You see a stool here.  On the workbench are a gold nugget, some bolts of cloth,
a needle, a chisel, and an idol.

>get all,pearl
stool: Taken.
gold nugget: Taken.
bolts of cloth: Taken.
needle: Taken.
chisel: Taken.
idol: Taken.
[[string]] of pearls: Taken.

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>e
Washroom
Sculpting is a dusty business.  You use this sink to clean off after a hard
day’s work.  Beside the sink is a small side table, and on the wall is a
calculator.  The rest of the studio is south and west.

On the side table are a manual and a comb.

>x sink
This is a state-of-the-art mop sink with anti-miasmic coating and bronze
backsplash.  It is so modern, there are no handles or other obvious ways to
turn it on.

An iron key is lodged in the drain.

>get key
Taken.

>s
At the Altar
Light from the window illuminates a crude altar.  Until recently, this area was
the gallery where customers would buy your art; all that is gone now.  The rest
of the studio lies north and west.

A pole sticks out of a wicker cage and leans ithyphallically against the wall.

>x window,net,window
window: It’s just a window above the altar.  The space under the window is
blank; as an interior [[decorator]], you can’t help but think the wall would
benefit from a fresco, but – sigh – you are too lovelorn to wield the brush.

pole: It is a [[long]] wooden pole with a bag attached to the end inside the
wicker cage.  This versatile tool can be used as a quarterstaff, butterfly net,
pool net, or walking stick.  There is something bulky in the bag, but you can’t
see what it is.

window: It’s just a window above the altar.  The wall right below it is a
boring [[white space]].

(Your score has just increased by three points.)

>give slab idol
Done.

>pray it
“O Aphrodite,” you say, “comforter of hopeless lovers, hear my prayer!  May she
to whom I have given my heart be given body, soul, and life.  And a colorful
personality.  And—”

You are interrupted by a shimmering about the altar.  As you watch, it takes
the form of a callipygian goddess.

“Mortal, I have heard your heart-felt and oft-repeated plea, and I will take
pity on you,” says Aphrodite.  “Prove your devotion by giving me three tokens
of your love as offerings, and I will give you the [[keyword]] of life.  Speak
this word in the presence of a mirror and your wish will be granted.”

She fades away, adding, “As for her colorful personality, just look around
you.”

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>g
Aphrodite reappears.  She eyes the idol skeptically.  “No [[comment]].”

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>give slab pearl
(first taking the idol from the altar)
Done.

>pray it
Aphrodite reappears.  “A string of pearls is a good start.”  The string of
pearls disappears in a bright flash.

>sew fur
You sew the bolts of cloth into a colorful chiton.

>give slab fur
Done.

>pray it
Aphrodite reappears.  “Passion imbues this chiton.  I am almost convinced.”
The chiton disappears in a bright flash.

>open cage,net
wicker cage:
(first unlocking the wicker cage)
Opened.

net: The net contains a mallet and a ball-peen hammer.

>get hammers,net,cage
ball-peen hammer: Taken.
mallet: Taken.
net: The net slips through the bars.
wicker cage: Taken.

>hit gold with peen
What should you make it into?  You can’t quite put your finger on it... that’s
it!  You beat the gold nugget with the ball-peen hammer and shape it into a
finger ring.  You hold it up and through it see your statue inaureoled across
the studio.

>give slab ring
Done.

>pray it
Aphrodite reappears.

“A gold ring!  Perfect!  With tokens like these, this must be true love.  Oh,
yes, the keyword: you’ll probably need to give it a focus.  Try carving the
catchphrase of fate somewhere near the object of your affections.”

The gold ring disappears in a bright flash.  When your eyes readjust, you see a
bronze key lying in its place.

>get key
You take the bronze key.

>n
Washroom
Sculpting is a dusty business.  You use this sink to clean off after a hard
day’s work.  Beside the sink is a small side table, and on the wall is a
calculator.  The rest of the studio is south and west.

On the side table are a manual and a comb.

>c +20000
The calculator outputs +20000 = 20000.  Water flows from the faucet, filling
the sink.

>put bronze,idol in sink
bronze key: You clean the bronze key, revealing a [[label]].

idol: Done.

(Your score has just increased by one point.)

>x addon,book,clean,sink
calculator: The calculator is [[built in]]to the wall beside the sink.  It has
buttons for all the standard unary and binary operations.  The screen reads
+20000 = 20000.

manual: [[Operator]]’s Manual

To control the auto-sink, use the calculator add-on to enter the desired volume
of water.  It supports the standard Thalassa++ unary and binary operations:

   + – addition
   - – subtraction
   * – multiplication
   / – division
   % – modulo
   ~ – bitwise NOT
   ! – logical NOT
   & – bitwise AND
   | – bitwise OR
   ^ – bitwise XOR
   << – shift left
   >> – arithmetic shift right
   >>> – logical shift right

For example,
       CALCULATE 69 TIMES 105
to fill the sink with 7,245 kochliaria.

Warning: Do not use big [[number]]s or divide by zero!

bronze key: It is a bronze key.  On it is etched the word “rhimon”.

sink: This is a state-of-the-art mop sink with anti-miasmic coating and bronze
backsplash.  It is so modern, there are no handles or other obvious ways to
turn it on.

It is full to the brim with water.

An idol is [[float]]ing on the surface of the water.

(Your score has just increased by four points.)

>c 1/0
The calculator outputs [[ERROR]] {division by zero}.  The water in the sink is
sucked down the drain.

